seg-2da07c5d32d7 = L-band waterfall, frequency across and time down. Arrow keys move a cursor over frequency and time; Escape leaves it.

# text
seg-46f65efc3be9 = The waterfall is drawn from the recorded run with JavaScript. The engine's report below shows the same run.

# text
# c1: l-band-waterfall-jamming.toml
seg-0f40f51945bf = Recorded run of <c1/> (seed { "7" }, engine { "v0.39.0" }): { "5" } GNSS bands, { "3" } jammers over { "60" } s, tracking floor { "25" } dB-Hz. Jammers: chirp privacy device at { "1,575.42" } MHz from { "10" } s to { "40" } s; CW tone on L1 at { "1,575.42" } MHz from { "30" } s to the end; L2 narrowband noise at { "1,227.60" } MHz from { "45" } s to the end.

# text
seg-45d6be782732 = GPS L1 C/A loses lock at { "10" } s and stays lost, lowest { "3.2" } dB-Hz. Galileo E1 loses lock at { "10" } s and recovers at { "40" } s, lowest { "4.4" } dB-Hz. GPS L2C tracks throughout, lowest { "36.9" } dB-Hz. GPS L5 tracks throughout, lowest { "44.1" } dB-Hz. Galileo E5a tracks throughout, lowest { "46.7" } dB-Hz.

# text
# c1: campaign-spectrum-holdover-integrity.toml
seg-ba40ce1e86f4 = The campaign it drives, <c1/> (seed { "20260928" }): L-band jamming from the spectrum, clock holdover and a Galileo-only fallback. Holdover for { "600" } s with the clock free-running, worst time error { "5.06" } ns against a { "50" } ns guard; then a Galileo-only fallback with a protection level of { "6.1" } to { "17.7" } m, under the { "50" } m alert limit.

